      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://aicoachellavalley.com/get-agent-ready/#faq",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "We already pay for SEO. Why do we need this?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Different budget, different layer. SEO optimizes for human eyes on Google search results pages — someone typing a query, clicking a blue link, landing on your site. That work still matters and it isn't what AICV does. AICV operates in the layer agents read when they answer a user's question directly, without surfacing a results page at all. When someone asks Claude or ChatGPT where to hold a corporate retreat in the Coachella Valley, your SEO ranking on Google is irrelevant to that answer. Your presence in the regional substrate agents query is what decides whether you're in the answer. Both budgets are legitimate. They serve different interfaces."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why is there a Deployment Fee separate from annual membership?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The Deployment Fee covers the work done once — the diagnostic, the node build, the MCP configuration, the Review (Tier 2), and the portal build. Annual membership keeps everything running. Pricing both honestly is cleaner than bundling setup cost into year-one dues and making year two feel overpriced."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does AICV touch our website?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. That's the point. AICV represents members at Tier 4 agent-readiness in parallel to their own sites — members don't modify their websites, change their CMS, or install anything. The work happens entirely in the substrate AICV operates."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens if we stop paying?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Your canonical node stays published at the Free AICV Listed tier — you remain discoverable. Agent-layer access (concierge, economic-development platform, templatized MCP tools) turns off. Your Agentic Review portal (Tier 2) goes private. Rejoining is straightforward; existing node data isn't lost."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Who qualifies for membership?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Any valley business, institution, property, or civic entity whose presence strengthens the Network's collective signal. AICV reserves editorial judgment on fit — the Network is a curated signal, not a directory."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can we see an example of the Agentic Review?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. The Visit Greater Palm Springs Snapshot at aicoachellavalley.com/snapshots/visit-greater-palm-springs is the public entry point of the same framework. The full Review deepens the three-dimension assessment, adds the 12-month roadmap, and lives as a portal that updates quarterly."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is AICV a nonprofit?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "AICV is a fiscally sponsored project of the Desert Community Foundation, a 501(c)(3) operating in Riverside County, California. Membership fees fund the continued build-out of the regional intelligence layer."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What's the founding-member cap actually protecting?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Two things. A bounded cohort whose pricing stays locked for life — a genuine reward for early commitment. And AICV's own delivery capacity: the first ten Tier 2 members are deployed and supported personally by Sat. Standard pricing begins at member eleven, by which point Network density, delivery tooling, and positioning have all matured."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What ships this summer?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Three things, together: the public Ask AICV chat interface, the AICV Network member directory (in development), and member-scoped query access for deployed members. Members who deploy before summer see themselves appear in all three as they ship."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "My business handles bookings or transactions. Will AICV support agent-mediated payments?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "AICV is tracking emerging agent-payment protocols, including Coinbase's x402 and the Agentic Commerce Protocol (ACP). For Premium members in transaction-driven categories — hospitality, dining, wellness, retail — AICV plans to deploy agent-payable MCP endpoints as the standards stabilize and member needs are scoped. This is part of the infrastructure differentiation between Agent Ready Business and Agent Ready Premium: Premium members participate in capability planning and receive priority deployment of new agentic commerce surfaces."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
